  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"10a\"><p><strong>10a</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>The object is not in equilibrium, because it is moving in a circle, so the direction of its velocity constantly changes.</p>\n<p>OR</p>\n<p>The object is not in equilibrium, because it is constantly changing direction.</p>\n<p>OR</p>\n<p>The object is not in equilibrium, because it has (centripetal) acceleration.</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"10b\"><p><strong>10b</strong></p><p> </p>\n<p>\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source markscheme diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure>\n</p>\n<p></p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"10c(i)\"><p><strong>10c(i)</strong></p><p></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"sin71^{o} = \\frac{mg}{T}\"></span> OR <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"cos19^{o} = \\frac{mg}{T}\"></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T \\approx 8.57\"></span> N <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\approx\"></span> 8.6 N</p>\n<p>(Calculated answer must be given to at least 3 s. f. in order to earn final mark)</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"10c(ii)\"><p><strong>10c(ii)</strong></p><p></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"sin19^{o} = \\frac{F_{cp}}{T}\"></span> OR <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"cos71^{o} = \\frac{F_{cp}}{T}\"></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{cp} \\approx 2.8\"></span> N</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r = \\frac{2.8}{0.826 \\times 1.71^{2}} \\approx 1.2\"></span> m</p>\n<p>(Answer must be given to 2 s. f. in order to earn final mark)</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"10c(iii)\"><p><strong>10c(iii)</strong></p><p><em></em></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v = 1.71 \\times 1.2 \\approx 2.05\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T = \\frac{2 \\pi \\times 1.2}{2.05} \\approx 3.7\"></span> s</p>\n<p></p></section>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>An object of mass 826 g is attached to a string and rotates at constant speed in a horizontal circle of radius <em>r</em>. The angle between the string and the ceiling is 71<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{o}\"></span>.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>a. Outline whether the object is in equilibrium.</p>\n<p>  [2]</p>\n<p>b. Draw a free-body diagram for the object at the position where it is shown on the diagram.</p>\n<p>  [2]</p>\n<p>c. The object rotates with an angular speed of 1.71 rad s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>i. Show that the tension in the string is 8.6 N.</p>\n<p>  [2]</p>\n<p>ii. Calculate <em>r</em>. Give your answer to an appropriate number of significant figures.</p>\n<p>  [3]</p>\n<p>iii.  Find the period of rotation of the object.</p>\n<p>  [2]</p>\n<p></p>\n<p></p>"
  },
